Make R_Suicide() abort instead of exiting.

A fatal R error (a GC consistency failure with _R_GC_FAIL_ON_ERROR_ set,
a C stack overflow while handling an error, a failed startup) ends in
Rstd_Suicide(), which prints one line and exits with status 2. libFuzzer
does notice a target that exits, but the report carries no stack trace
and every such exit deduplicates to the same signature. abort() instead:
the sanitizer runtime prints where it happened and ClusterFuzz files it
under that location.

Instrumentation, not a fix: adapted from kevinushey/r-afl
(suicide-abort.patch). Not for upstream.

diff --git a/src/unix/sys-std.c b/src/unix/sys-std.c
index f86c2672d6..1a5c066687 100644
--- a/src/unix/sys-std.c
+++ b/src/unix/sys-std.c
@@ -70,8 +70,10 @@ extern FILE* ifp; /* from system.c */
 attribute_hidden void Rstd_Suicide(const char *s)
 {
     REprintf("Fatal error: %s\n", s);
-    /* Might be called before translation is running */
-    R_CleanUp(SA_SUICIDE, 2, 0);
+    /* A clean exit(2) would end the fuzzing process with no trace of
+       where the fatal error came from; abort() gets a stack trace from the
+       sanitizer runtime and deduplicates on it. */
+    abort();
 }
 
